  "status": "formal",
  "supportedClaim": "For the frozen exact-shear family, the signed heat-scale production observables vanish pointwise at every positive heat scale, while the heat-gradient covariance is strictly positive and the normalized positive exterior-size quantity is amplitude-cubic; therefore a finite amplitude-independent coercive modulus built only from zero-preserving operations on those production observables cannot control this family."
}
